  "notes": {
    "title": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -300,
      "maxW": 4240,
      "text": "Tasks · When and Deadline at a glance"
    },
    "howto": {
      "x": -560,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 480,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "How to try it\n\n• Press Play, then click inside once so it has the keys.\n• Picked: the When is quiet grey text, only a deadline is a capsule; the checkbox ring is red when overdue, amber when due today, blue when planned for today.\n• Proposed, on the strip: Wording, Planned + due, and When at (an experiment). The defaults are the recommendations, except When at, which stays right until you pick.\n• Hover a date for its full date; click it for the popover."
    },
    "t_cues": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 900,
      "maxW": 4240,
      "text": "1 · The checkbox rings: planned for today with a deadline (proposed)"
    },
    "n_cues": {
      "x": -560,
      "y": 1200,
      "w": 480,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "Picked: the ring is red when overdue, amber when due today, blue when the task is on today's plate (seen in a list).\n\nA deadline is past or today, never both, so the only clash is blue with red or amber.\n\nDouble ring (recommended): the deadline's ring outside, a thin blue ring inside. Both stay at the checkbox, where the user put the cues, and the deadline keeps the outer, stronger ring.\n\nSplit: half and half reads as two states, but at 16pt it looks broken. Blue moves to the When: quiet, but the plan leaves the checkbox, and in Today there's no When to carry it."
    },
    "t_place": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4320,
      "maxW": 4240,
      "text": "2 · The When aligned left (experiment)"
    },
    "n_place": {
      "x": -560,
      "y": 4620,
      "w": 480,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "After the title (recommended): the When reads with the title, after its notes hint, and the right edge holds only deadlines, so a scan down it finds every one. One line per row. At narrow widths the When drops before the title goes under 120pt.\n\nColumn: lines Whens up, but takes 84pt from every title, dated or not; beside the detail pane the median title loses a third.\n\nBelow the title: never competes for width, and never drops; but a dated row is 14pt taller, so the list's rhythm goes uneven (28% taller on School)."
    },
    "t_words": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 7740,
      "maxW": 5320,
      "text": "3 · Wording: “Nd left” to 14 days, then the date (proposed)"
    },
    "n_words": {
      "x": -560,
      "y": 8040,
      "w": 480,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "A deadline counts whole days left, not its own day: “14d left” … “1d left”, “Due today”, then “2d ago” (days at any distance, “16d ago”). Farther than 14 days it's the date: “Nov 15”, “Jan 3, 2027”.\n\nThe When follows the same rule as a plan: “Today”, “Tomorrow”, “in 2d” … “in 14d”, then the date.\n\nThe tooltip and the detail pane say it in words: “13 days left”, “2 days overdue”."
    },
    "t_views": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 11160,
      "maxW": 3240,
      "text": "Views and narrow widths"
    },
    "t_detail": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 12500,
      "maxW": 4240,
      "text": "The detail pane and the popover"
    }
  }
